{"text": "You have only three types of people in your life.\n\nFirst are the leaf people. They come for one season. They laugh beside you while the sun is out, and when the wind changes they are gone. A leaf was never built to stay through a storm.\n\nSecond are the branch people. They are stronger. For a while you can lean on them. But test a branch before you put your whole weight on it, my friend. Some hold for years. Some break the moment life turns heavy.\n\nAnd then there are the root people. These are rare. They do not stand where the light is. They do not help you so that others can watch them helping. They hold you up, underground, where nobody claps.\n\nComment roots, and I will send you the practice for finding yours.\n\nThe hard part is this. Most people spend their lives collecting leaves and calling it a forest. Counting your people is easy. Becoming a root for someone else is the work of years. Everything I know is inside The Quiet Between Thoughts. The link is in my profile.", "alignment": {"characters": ["Y", "o", "u", " ", "h", "a", "v", "e", " ", "o", "n", "l", "y", " ", "t", "h", "r", "e", "e", " ", "t", "y", "p", "e", "s", " ", "o", "f", " ", "p", "e", "o", "p", "l", "e", " ", "i", "n", " ", "y", "o", "u", "r", " ", "l", "i", "f", "e", ".", "\n", "\n", "F", "i", "r", "s", "t", " ", "a", "r", "e", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "l", "e", "a", "f", " ", "p", "e", "o", "p", "l", "e", ".", " ", "T", "h", "e", "y", " ", "c", "o", "m", "e", " ", "f", "o", "r", " ", "o", "n", "e", " ", "s", "e", "a", "s", "o", "n", ".", " ", "T", "h", "e", "y", " ", "l", "a", "u", "g", "h", " ", "b", "e", "s", "i", "d", "e", " ", "y", "o", "u", " ", "w", "h", "i", "l", "e", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "s", "u", "n", " ", "i", "s", " ", "o", "u", "t", ",", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "w", "h", "e", "n", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "w", "i", "n", "d", " ", "c", "h", "a", "n", "g", "e", "s", " ", "t", "h", "e", "y", " ", "a", "r", "e", " ", "g", "o", "n", "e", ".", " ", "A", " ", "l", "